# Build 9 stock-xradio and G2D acceptance

This generated kit accepts exactly Build 9 raw `@IMAGE_SHA@`. It is one
`kit-resume-boot-open`, three ordered `kit-resume-step` rows, and one
`kit-resume-close`. Do not add `ExtraBootArgs`, `KitPayload`, `insmod`, or a
serial data path. DutExec is used once for bounded bootstrap control; every
test byte and result moves over authenticated Wi-Fi SSH.

## Inputs and refusal gate

```bash
set -euo pipefail
expected_raw=@IMAGE_SHA@
generation=$(openssl rand -hex 16)
kit=${BUILD9_KIT:?generated raw-bound kit}
image_dir=${BUILD9_IMAGE_DIR:?published Build 9 image directory}
image=$image_dir/Image.img
image_source=$image_dir/ImageSource.json
live_repo=${PF_AUTOMATION_REPO:?merged pocketforge-automation checkout}
expected_automation=dcee1dfc258091984e70e62305c2c86e5544efae
seed_source=/home/matt/recovery/tsp-mc9m.41.995.43.3/kits/build8-writeback-standalone-r19
run_root=${BUILD9_RUN_ROOT:?recovery directory outside the generated kit}
run=$run_root/build9-accept-$generation
seed_kit=$run/seed-kit
SQ_DIR=/home/matt/recovery/gpu14
SQ_QUEUE=$SQ_DIR/queue.tsv
host_wifi_interface=wlp4s0
dut_interface=wlan0
wifi_source=${BUILD9_WIFI_SOURCE:-192.168.86.235}
laptop_ip=$wifi_source

test "$(git -C "$live_repo" rev-parse HEAD)" = "$expected_automation"
test "$(jq -r .RawSHA256 "$image_source")" = "$expected_raw"
test "$(sha256sum "$image" | cut -d' ' -f1)" = "$expected_raw"
test "$(sed -n 's/^build9_raw_sha256=//p' "$kit/IDENTITY")" = "$expected_raw"
(cd "$kit" && sha256sum -c --strict --quiet SHA256SUMS)
env PATH=/usr/bin:/bin "$kit/smoke.sh"
mkdir -p "$run/requests" "$run/series" "$run/row-receipts" "$run/revisions"
```

Any mismatch above is `BUILD9_STOP state=STOP stage=preflight
reason=raw_identity_mismatch`; do not read secrets, seal, or queue it.

## Fresh network-only seed and boot-open

The preparer is the network-only seed pattern from automation PR #1440. Its
payload argument is copied only as inert provenance; `--network-only` removes
`KitPayload` from the FelBoot request. Use the consumed r19 handle recorded in
that source kit. The final sealer call is the first secret/node mutation.

```bash
python3 "$kit/prepare-seed-template.py" --network-only \
  --source "$seed_source" --output "$seed_kit" \
  --payload "$kit/pf-kit-payload.tar.gz" --image-source "$image_source" \
  --consumed-handle 183b36e3dc8474620e948abfe12e469f
(cd "$seed_kit" && sha256sum -c --strict --quiet SHA256SUMS)
env PATH=/usr/bin:/bin "$seed_kit/postseal-check.sh" "$image" "$expected_raw"
install -d -m 0700 "$run/seed-transport"
python3 "$seed_kit/seal-request.py" --kit "$seed_kit" --image "$image" \
  --image-sha256 "$expected_raw" --transport-receipt-dir "$run/seed-transport"
felboot_request=$seed_kit/felboot-request.json
jq -e --arg raw "$expected_raw" \
  '(keys|sort)==["ImageSource","SeedHandle"] and .ImageSource.RawSHA256==$raw and
   (has("ExtraBootArgs")|not) and (has("KitPayload")|not)' \
  "$felboot_request" >/dev/null

deadline=$(date -u -d '+100 minutes' +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
anchor=$run/series/anchor.json
jq -n --arg anchor "$anchor" --arg repo "$live_repo" --arg generation "$generation" \
  --arg holder "tsp-mc9m.41.1002.8.8.$generation" --arg deadline "$deadline" \
  --arg original "$run/series/initial-flash.json" --arg kit "$kit" \
  --slurpfile image "$image_source" --slurpfile felboot "$felboot_request" \
  '{Anchor:$anchor,Live:{Repo:$repo},Generation:$generation,Holder:$holder,
    Dut:"tsp",Place:"tsp-base",Deadline:$deadline,ImageSource:$image[0],
    FelBootRequest:$felboot[0],OriginalBootReceipt:$original,
    BaseKitDirectory:$kit}' >"$run/requests/boot-open.json"
env SQ_DIR="$SQ_DIR" SQ_QUEUE="$SQ_QUEUE" "$SQ_DIR/seal-resume-row.sh" \
  "build9-accept-boot-open-$generation" kit-resume-boot-open \
  "$run/requests/boot-open.json" "$run/row-receipts/boot-open" './smoke.sh'
```

Wait for the anchor, then prove the complete image was written and read back:

```bash
jq -e --arg raw "$expected_raw" --arg original "$run/series/initial-flash.json" \
  '.BaseImageRawSHA256Verified==$raw and .OriginalBootReceiptPath==$original' \
  "$anchor" >/dev/null
jq -e --arg raw "$expected_raw" \
  '.TaskState=="Completed" and .ReturnCode==0 and
   .SourceVerification.Write.RawSHA256==$raw and
   .SourceVerification.Readback.RawSHA256==$raw' \
  "$run/series/initial-flash.json" >/dev/null
```

## Ordered steps

```bash
make_revision() {
  name=$1; dst=$run/revisions/$name
  mkdir "$dst"; cp -a "$kit/." "$dst/"; printf '%s\n' "$name" >"$dst/REVISION"
  (cd "$dst"; find . -maxdepth 1 -type f ! -name SHA256SUMS -printf '%P\n' |
    sort | while read -r file; do sha256sum "$file"; done >SHA256SUMS;
    sha256sum -c --strict --quiet SHA256SUMS)
}
queue_step() {
  name=$1; request=$2
  env SQ_DIR="$SQ_DIR" SQ_QUEUE="$SQ_QUEUE" "$SQ_DIR/seal-resume-row.sh" \
    "build9-accept-$name-$generation" kit-resume-step "$request" \
    "$run/row-receipts/$name" './smoke.sh'
}
```

Revision 000 is the only DutExec row. It confirms stock in-tree xradio, no
blacklist, completed CCMP association, DHCPv4, default route, SSH listener, and
returns the fresh public host key. A command refusal is INVALID, never FAIL.

```bash
make_revision bootstrap
jq -n --arg anchor "$anchor" --arg repo "$live_repo" \
  --arg receipt "$run/series/revision-000.json" --arg kit "$run/revisions/bootstrap" \
  --rawfile cmd "$kit/bootstrap-dut.sh" --slurpfile image "$image_source" \
  '{Anchor:$anchor,Live:{Repo:$repo},Receipt:$receipt,ImageSource:$image[0],
    RevisionDirectory:$kit,Steps:[{Name:"network-bootstrap",Transport:"dutexec",
    Command:$cmd}],Final:false}' >"$run/requests/bootstrap.json"
queue_step bootstrap "$run/requests/bootstrap.json"
bootstrap=$run/series/revision-000.json
jq -e --arg dut "$dut_interface" '.Outcome=="pass" and (.StepResults|map(.Name))==["network-bootstrap"] and
  (.StepResults[0].Stdout|test("BUILD9_BOOTSTRAP state=PASS dut_interface="+$dut+" address=[0-9.]+ stock_xradio=in-tree extra_boot_args=absent ssh=active"))' \
  "$bootstrap" >/dev/null
dut_host=$(jq -r '.StepResults[0].Stdout|capture("address=(?<a>[0-9.]+)").a' "$bootstrap")
jq -r '.StepResults[0].Stdout|split("\n")[]|select(startswith("ssh-ed25519 "))' \
  "$bootstrap" | awk -v h="$dut_host" '{print h" "$0}' >"$run/known_hosts"
chmod 0600 "$run/known_hosts"
known_sha=$(sha256sum "$run/known_hosts" | cut -d' ' -f1)
```

Revision 001 is network-only. It asserts host `wlp4s0` association and its
direct route, then proves authenticated SSH with helper receipts and performs
push -> push-exec -> pull for the deterministic 1 MiB object.

```bash
make_revision network
jq -n --arg anchor "$anchor" --arg repo "$live_repo" \
  --arg receipt "$run/series/revision-001.json" --arg kit "$run/revisions/network" \
  --arg host "$dut_host" --arg receipts "$run/seed-transport" \
  --arg known "$run/known_hosts" --arg known_sha "$known_sha" \
  --arg iface "$host_wifi_interface" --arg dut_iface "$dut_interface" --arg source "$wifi_source" --arg laptop "$laptop_ip" \
  --slurpfile image "$image_source" \
  '{Anchor:$anchor,Live:{Repo:$repo},Receipt:$receipt,ImageSource:$image[0],
    RevisionDirectory:$kit,Steps:[{Name:"network",Transport:"network",
    Argv:[$kit+"/run-network-step",$host,"debug",$receipts,$known,$known_sha,
    $iface,$source,$laptop,$dut_iface]}],Final:false}' >"$run/requests/network.json"
queue_step network "$run/requests/network.json"
jq -e '.Outcome=="pass" and (.StepResults|map(.Name))==["network"] and
  (.StepResults[0].Stdout|contains("BUILD9_NETWORK_STEP state=PASS host_interface=wlp4s0") and contains("transport=network-only"))' \
  "$run/series/revision-001.json" >/dev/null
grep -Eq "^BUILD9_NETWORK state=PASS dut_interface=${dut_interface} address=[0-9.]+ route=default authenticated_ssh=pass root_pings=pass$" "$run/seed-transport/pull-12/network-result.txt"
grep -Fx 'BUILD9_TRANSPORT state=PASS operation=push-push-exec-pull bytes=1048576 sha256=30e14955ebf1352266dc2ff8067e68104607e750abb9d3b36582b8af909fcb58' "$run/seed-transport/pull-12/network-result.txt"
```

Revision 002 carries the unchanged G2D payload and all results over that same
network leg. Its predicates are copied verbatim from template manifest
`730aefb67e125ae49674674c0d93e26353a644eec556060cc63e5480ed341792`.

```bash
make_revision g2d
jq -n --arg anchor "$anchor" --arg repo "$live_repo" \
  --arg receipt "$run/series/revision-002.json" --arg kit "$run/revisions/g2d" \
  --arg host "$dut_host" --arg receipts "$run/seed-transport" \
  --arg known "$run/known_hosts" --arg known_sha "$known_sha" \
  --slurpfile image "$image_source" \
  '{Anchor:$anchor,Live:{Repo:$repo},Receipt:$receipt,ImageSource:$image[0],
    RevisionDirectory:$kit,Steps:[{Name:"g2d",Transport:"network",
    Argv:[$kit+"/run-g2d-step",$host,"debug",$receipts,$known,$known_sha]}],
    Final:true}' >"$run/requests/g2d.json"
queue_step g2d "$run/requests/g2d.json"
jq -e '.Outcome=="pass" and (.StepResults|map(.Name))==["g2d"] and
  (.StepResults[0].Stdout=="BUILD9_G2D_STEP state=PASS transport=network-only payload=push execution=push-exec results=pull\n")' \
  "$run/series/revision-002.json" >/dev/null
```

## Close and exact stop predicates

Always queue close after an opened series, including after STOP, INVALID, or
FAIL. VBUS isolation must be proven before graceful poweroff; no fallback is a
successful acceptance close.

```bash
python3 "$kit/pf-kit-transport.py" teardown-key --receipt-dir "$run/seed-transport"
jq -n --arg anchor "$anchor" --arg repo "$live_repo" \
  --arg receipt "$run/series/terminal.json" \
  '{Anchor:$anchor,Live:{Repo:$repo},Receipt:$receipt,Reason:"success"}' \
  >"$run/requests/close.json"
env SQ_DIR="$SQ_DIR" SQ_QUEUE="$SQ_QUEUE" "$SQ_DIR/seal-resume-row.sh" \
  "build9-accept-close-$generation" kit-resume-close "$run/requests/close.json" \
  "$run/row-receipts/close" -
jq -e '.Schema=="pocketforge.kit-resume-terminal/v1" and .State=="CLOSED" and
  .Reason=="success" and (.Teardown|map(.Action))==
  ["vbus-off","graceful-poweroff","force-off","psu-off","power-zero","reap","lease-release","place-free"] and
  (.Teardown|all(.Status=="pass"))' "$run/series/terminal.json" >/dev/null
```

Classification is exact: `BUILD9_NETWORK state=INVALID ...
reason=instrument_refused` means the instrument refused a root operation and
the device verdict is unmade; `BUILD9_STOP state=STOP stage=<bootstrap|network|g2d>
reason=<token>` means a prerequisite or transport predicate was not proved;
`BUILD9_NETWORK state=FAIL ...` is reserved for an executed root data-path
probe that returned failure. No class permits serial fallback or continuation
to G2D. Before live queueing, rerun `dut-binary-check.sh` against this published
image for all generated DUT commands, run `smoke.sh`, and `jq -e .` every
request. `seal-resume-row.sh` mutates the queue and has no dry run.
